--- Selects between two branches based on a predicate.
---
--- @details
--- `choice` takes `[value, pred, true_fn, false_fn]`. If `pred(value)`
--- is truthy, `true_fn(value)` is returned; otherwise `false_fn(value)`.
--- Both branches receive the same `value`, so `choice` expresses a
--- conditional *transformation* rather than a conditional *statement* —
--- the result is whichever branch computes.
---
--- For one-sided transforms (keep `value` when the predicate fails),
--- use `comb.when` / `comb.unless` instead.
---
--- @example
--- `[4, x ~> x % 2 == 0, x ~> "even", x ~> "odd"] >>> comb.choice`
--- -- => "even"
---
export choice :: [value, pred, true_fn, false_fn] ~> {
  if pred(value) {
    true_fn(value)
  } else {
    false_fn(value)
  }
}
